id: stance
name: Stance
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/round
# A Special Maneuver, open while Martial Skill is had (`allow maneuver.stance`). Used: one of the four Stances taken - or none -
# in place of the one held (conditions.mjs takeOneCondition); each a mark of its own beside it (conditions/).
special: true
# Core Rule, so every character has its Item, shut until Martial Skill opens it - as every Special Maneuver an effect grants.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Enter a Stance - Flame, Wind, Wave or Stone - or leave the one you are in. One at a time.
text: >
  Stance Maneuver [1/Round]: You shift your footing and center your body to take a combat stance.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Upon using this effect, enter a Stance. If you use this Maneuver while already in a Stance, you may leave a Stance or enter another Stance of your choice. Your maximum number of concurrent Stances is 1; to enter a Stance when at your maximum number of concurrent Stances you must replace one of those Stances with the new Stance you intend to enter. There are 4 Stances:
  • Flame Stance. Increase your Wound Rolls and Might by 1(T), but reduce your Awareness by 1(T).
  • Wind Stance. Increase your Defense Value and Speeds by 1(T), but reduce your Soak Value by 1(T).
  • Wave Stance. Increase your Awareness and Impulsive/Corporeal Saves by 1(T), but reduce your Wound Rolls by 2(T).
  • Stone Stance. Increase your Soak Value and Surgency by 1(T), but reduce your Defense Value by 1(T).

---

[on used]
takeOneCondition(flame-stance, wind-stance, wave-stance, stone-stance);
